From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:08:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - drain region work and close storage when a
 world unloads

A world being unloaded stops ticking its regions, and the work queued
on them was abandoned: entity schedulers neither ran nor retired their
tasks (Folia promises one of the two), region scheduler tasks stayed
IDLE forever and queued region tasks kept their runnables. After the
chunks are saved, the world's shutdown thread now retires every entity
scheduler holding tasks (invoking the retired callbacks), cancels the
region scheduler tasks and cancels the queued region tasks without
running them (WorldUnloadDrain).

The world's region storage was closed only by the last region's chunk
save, so a world unloaded with no region kept its region files open,
and an Aurora World Fabric world its stores and Redis lease, until the
server stopped. Without a region the storage is now flushed and closed
directly.

diff --git a/dev/iyanz/aurora/engine/threadedregions/WorldShutdownThread.java b/dev/iyanz/aurora/engine/threadedregions/WorldShutdownThread.java
index b6be665b27fbd0a7bce198b52c9793a164a6a07a..b325336584a632ab4ffffb82bb4fc58c47cac941 100644
--- a/dev/iyanz/aurora/engine/threadedregions/WorldShutdownThread.java
+++ b/dev/iyanz/aurora/engine/threadedregions/WorldShutdownThread.java
@@ -58,7 +58,8 @@ public class WorldShutdownThread extends RegionShutdownThread {
     @Override
     public void run() {
         // SourbyCraft start - always complete the unload callback, also when the unload throws
-        WorldUnloadCompletion.run(this.level.canvas$unloadTicket::get, this::unload);
+        WorldUnloadCompletion.run(this.level.canvas$unloadTicket::get, this::unload,
+            () -> WorldUnloadDrain.releaseBridgedTasks(this.level, this.debugName, LOGGER)); // SourbyCraft - release bridged tasks also when the unload throws
     }
 
     private void unload() {
@@ -183,6 +184,8 @@ public class WorldShutdownThread extends RegionShutdownThread {
                     region = regions.get(i);
                 saveRegionChunks(region, (i + 1) == regions.size());
             }
+            // SourbyCraft - the last region's save closes the world's storage; without a region it must be closed here
+            WorldUnloadDrain.closeStorageWithoutRegions(this.level, regions.size());
         } catch (final Throwable thrown) {
             LOGGER.error("Failed to save chunks in {}", getWorldName(), thrown);
             throw thrown;
@@ -190,6 +193,9 @@ public class WorldShutdownThread extends RegionShutdownThread {
             LOGGER.info("Saved chunks in {}", getWorldName());
         }
 
+        // SourbyCraft - retire entity schedulers, cancel region scheduler and queued region tasks
+        WorldUnloadDrain.drain(this, this.level, regions, LOGGER);
+
         // now we save level data and force pearl data save
 
         saveLevelData(this.level);
diff --git a/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedTaskQueue.java b/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/RegionizedTaskQueue.java
index e66ce540744b9a93d0505dbb875d5e55d5009a1c..2ae2b9799bc3709dbea96f1d1cd86bf72b6d605c 100644
